{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>To lie by her, to be with her.</b> Rashi explained: 'to lie by her' — even without intercourse. For perhaps there is a distinction between 'by her' and 'with her,' yet in any case she demanded this, for if not, who sought this from him? And perhaps there is support for this from what is written (Genesis 39:10): ״וַיְהִי כְּדַבְּרָהּ אֶל יוֹסֵף יוֹם יוֹם״ — and it did not specify what she said; rather, surely this is its meaning: For at first she said, 'Lie with me' literally — ״וַיְמָאֵן״ etc. — and afterward she sought to diminish it: to lie by her without intercourse. And should he fear that perhaps this closeness would lead to the act itself — regarding this she said, 'See, it is daytime now, and it is not the way of the world to have relations by day' — and he did not listen to her. And afterward she sought to diminish further: that he be secluded with her in a room, for there is no concern about the act since, as stated, it is day. This is what it says: ״כְּדַבְּרָהּ אֶל יוֹסֵף יוֹם יוֹם״ — that she asked two requests one after the other, and both of them by day. And he did not listen to her, neither to the first request — to lie by her without intercourse — nor to the second request — to be with her in a single room. ״וַיְהִי כְהַיּוֹם הַזֶּה״ (Genesis 39:11) — in the very heart of the day; he was not afraid lest she seek the act from him, for she had already said that their way is not to have relations by day. Therefore ״וַיָּבֹא הַבַּיְתָה לַעֲשׂוֹת מְלַאכְתּוֹ״ (Genesis 39:11) — even though he did not wish even to be secluded with her, that was when he was idle from work; but now that he went to do his work, Joseph thought that she would not seek anything from him, so as not to cause him to neglect the work of the house — for her husband would hang the blame on her, saying, 'Why did you not spur the slave on to the work?' Even so, ״וַתִּתְפְּשֵׂהוּ בְּבִגְדוֹ״ (Genesis 39:12), and she returned to the first request, saying, 'Lie with me' literally."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:39.660436650Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}